              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 120,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "purple",
                "label": "Bat"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 410,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 130,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "Cat"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 150,
                "text": "1 bone → 2 bones → wrist → digits",
                "size": 22,
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 210,
                "text": "same structure, different jobs",
                "size": 20,
                "anchor": "middle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Related species became different to suit different places. That is divergent evolution.",
          "write": "divergent evolution"
        },
        {
          "say": "Analogous structures do the same job but are built differently.",
          "write": "analogous = same function"
        },
        {
          "say": "Bird and insect wings both fly, but evolved separately. That is convergent evolution.",
          "write": "convergent evolution"
        },
        {
          "say": "Vestigial structures are reduced leftovers, like a whale pelvis or our tailbone.",
          "write": "vestigial structures"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Evidence from molecules",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "All life uses DNA, the same four bases and almost the same code.",
          "write": "one common origin"
        },
        {
          "say": "We line up DNA or protein sequences, like cytochrome c, and count differences.",
          "write": "count differences"
        },
        {
          "say": "Fewer differences means a more recent common ancestor.",
          "write": "fewer diffs = closer"
        },
        {
          "say": "Mutations build up at a roughly steady rate. That is the molecular clock.",
          "write": "molecular clock"
        },
        {
          "say": "Calibrate it with dated fossils, and it estimates when lineages split.",
          "write": "fossils calibrate"
        },
        {
          "say": "DNA shows more differences than protein, because the code is degenerate.",
          "write": "silent mutations"
        }
      ]
    },
